text:
elaine: quick pass on an Ember-Slate dark theme — dropped frames + a tiny CSS vars update in the PR. figma link: https://www.figma.com/file/ember-slate

mike: nice direction. quick visual nit: axis ticks read a little lime against panels. current is #9ad586 and feels too lively.

jess: agree, less green. maybe a desaturated slate blue like #6b8ea3

ryan_frontend: threw up a preview branch `/deploy-preview/621`. updated vars snippet below:

```
:root {
  --bg: #070b0e;
  --panel: #0d1216;
  --text: #d9e8ef;
  --axis: #6b8ea3;
  --muted: #909ca6;
}
```

omar_a11y: accessibility flag: small helper text (11px) on panel (#0d1216) with --muted (#909ca6) is 3.7:1. body text needs >=4.5:1. options: bump to 12px, bold at 600, or shift to #b0c4cf

elaine: for speed let's bold helper text and re-run checks. also chart hairlines are lost in dark at 1px; increase to 1.5px and use subtle border rgba(220,230,238,0.05)

ryan_frontend: implemented lineWidth: 1.5 and gridColor: rgba(220,230,238,0.04). switched axis to #6b8ea3 in preview. preview link: /deploy-preview/621

mike: syntax highlight question: functions are teal which clashes with sparkline. current code palette: keywords #d6a57a, functions #6fd1b0, strings #d8ad90, comments #6f7e86

jess: move functions away from teal. propose steel #5f90a4 for functions, keep keywords warm gold. reduces competition with metrics

omar_a11y: re-ran local checks after swapping functions to #5f90a4. results: inline code 4.8, comments 4.1, helper (bolded) 4.6. good improvement.

theme-bot: scheduled light internal AB: ember-slate-A (current) vs ember-slate-B (tweaks) for 36h, 40 users per bucket. will capture task clarity and tooltip discovery

elaine: also quick thought on heatmap gradient: want lows very dark so small values don't pop. proposal: #03060a -> #123042 -> #5f90a4 -> #cfe7ff. happy to iterate after run

ryan_frontend: noted. i'll open the PR with vars + chart defaults. thanks all :sparkles:
